#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129959} :activity/id #uuid "6b5e9ddb-fece-505f-9038-e2889dc1bb41" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049313 :topic/id #uuid "eb878fef-0b1e-5195-86ee-dbbe55f58094" :topic/math-academy-id 2033} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129959 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130345 :tutorial/content "To plot the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nwe first create a table of values.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\dfrac{1}{x}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $\\text{undefined}$ | $4$ | $2$ | $1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThen, we draw the graph by plotting the corresponding $(x,y)$ pairs and connecting them.\n\n![](images/3e/3eea82487a56147789d1c383c21e37c447dc94d735de094acd80183894462a38.png)\n\nThis type of curve is called a **rectangular hyperbola.**" :tutorial/id #uuid "fd012276-cc15-5f66-98e5-8c9207880e8d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3459 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "7d340241-a641-511e-8b12-d41dbbf0aed2" :step/math-academy-id 19590 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129962}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129960 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129125 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128936 :question/id #uuid "0203f79c-5170-51ac-8255-748dfd579c24" :question/math-academy-id "e-5297"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99c4151a-d2e0-5603-b27d-d81c76a0c7ba" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049072} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049078} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050255} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050580}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129416} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129714} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234018}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Reciprocal Curves"} :step/id #uuid "eef9e249-4d3a-5829-be7c-bdeae66590b2" :step/math-academy-id 19592} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129961 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129126 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128937 :question/id #uuid "3097e092-5889-5eab-9561-e331f2f71023" :question/math-academy-id "e-5298"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "27c4ce4c-7b03-5d9e-a1f0-be891c40f6a0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048838}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129716} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129835}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Graph of a Reciprocal Function"} :step/id #uuid "b87955b0-87da-5f68-bff3-5fe930889279" :step/math-academy-id 19593 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130148}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129962 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130346 :tutorial/content "Let's now plot the graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nOnce again, we first create a table of values.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $-\\dfrac{1}{x}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ | $\\text{undefined}$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $-\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n\nNow, we can plot the graph:\n\n![](images/9a/9af11caef6739f83d32e0190ddc89c98b8e0150aa430184ee5e234a7febe8d8a.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nis the reflection of the curve\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nover the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/50/507a0a5cf7c2a1871efd76092c5164424ce17f3425c1bfc33df89cecefa81803.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "25766180-7f5a-5dcd-a146-623a8a328eed" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3460 :tutorial/title "The Graph of a Negative Reciprocal Curve"} :step/id #uuid "b2df8185-e92c-5281-a5be-2370aa2ea056" :step/math-academy-id 19594 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129961}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130148 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130430 :tutorial/content "Let's sketch the curve\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac1x\n$$\n\n![](images/ff/ffd98b8f9b6c7a9260f43772f9c654901bd02c21efa1eb06f2a5fdad8b263729.png)\n\nThere are some key points to note about this curve:\n\n- As $x \\to 0^+$, the graph approaches $\\infty$.\n- As $x \\to 0^-$, the graph approaches $-\\infty$.\n- The graph has the *vertical asymptote* $x=0$.\n- As $x\\to\\infty$ or $x\\to-\\infty$, the graph approaches the *horizontal asymptote* $y=0$.\n- The domain is $x\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$, and the range is $y\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- The function is a decreasing function." :tutorial/id #uuid "90ffa0d5-a0de-5274-98f7-14be1211cb8f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5921 :tutorial/title "Properties of the Reciprocal Curve"} :step/id #uuid "b3bbaae9-e641-5989-8156-0d5597d05c70" :step/math-academy-id 36161 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130149}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130149 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130431 :tutorial/content "Now let's remind ourselves of the graph of\n\n$$\ny = -\\dfrac1x\n$$\n\n![](images/e3/e3f5ed500c81d09e2775f09fd10a221d7ec0fca7e39249b7add7a680328b68c1.png)\n\nThere are some key points to note about this curve:\n\n- As $x\\to 0^+$, the graph approaches $-\\infty$.\n- As $x \\to 0^-$, the graph approaches $\\infty$.\n- The graph has the *vertical asymptote* $x=0$.\n- As $x\\to\\infty$ or $x\\to-\\infty$, the graph approaches the *horizontal asymptote* $y=0$.\n- The domain is $x\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$, and the range is $y\\in(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- The function is an increasing function." :tutorial/id #uuid "53cfe059-da8c-5dab-bed6-35410a72f2d2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5922 :tutorial/title "Properties of the Negative Reciprocal Curve"} :step/id #uuid "6ad79a4c-2888-590a-9b45-d98bcf3f6d8e" :step/math-academy-id 36162 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129960}}] :activity/title "Graphing Reciprocal Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186129372}]}
